Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] core: select certified AOP reload through DT

A retained AOP must not be reset as though it were a fresh boot. Select
retained reload through device-tree data, preserving ordinary
initialization for other hardware.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/printk/printk.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/printk/printk.c b/kernel/printk/printk.c
index 3fcdf4b4e..fcc51b699 100644
--- a/kernel/printk/printk.c
+++ b/kernel/printk/printk.c
@@ -4589,6 +4589,7 @@ bool pr_flush(int timeout_ms, bool reset_on_progress)
 {
 	return __pr_flush(NULL, timeout_ms, reset_on_progress);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pr_flush);
 
 /*
  * Delayed printk version, for scheduler-internal messages:
